  notes: |
    Mobile sticky strip (≤720px) of 14 Strudel mini-notation snippet
    buttons (note(, s(, stack(, n(, <, >, [, ], *, ?, .gain(, .lpf(, ,,
    space). Each tap inserts the snippet at the cursor (or replaces
    the selected range) via CodeMirror's EditorView.dispatch; cursor
    is parked right after insertion. Editor focus is restored after
    each tap so the native VKB keeps the editor context.

    CodeMirrorEditor exposes an imperative onReady(api) handle so
    external components (the toolbar) can dispatch through the same
    view.dispatch — goes through the existing updateListener, so
    replaceScore → IDB save → undo history all keep working unchanged.

    Hidden on desktop (≥721px) via @media. On mobile when native VKB
    opens, toolbar floats above it using --visual-viewport-height
    CSS var updated by a debounced (100ms) window.visualViewport
    resize listener.

    Unit tests (vitest): 10 tests covering insert-at-cursor,
    replace-selection, single-char operators, space insert, undo/
    redo round-trip, empty-doc edge cases, snippet-table invariants.
    E2E (playwright): 2 specs — mobile (375×667) insert + desktop
    (1280) hidden.

    Quality gates: pnpm run lint, typecheck, test:run — all clean.
